{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.collatz_contact_boundary","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.collatz_contact_boundary","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.qou_obstruction_reduction"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.collatz_contact_boundary","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.collatz_contact_boundary","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/collatz_contact_boundary.lean#L68-L135","doc":"**Manuscript statement** (full body):\n\n**Proposition (within a QOU with `2 ∣ χ(A)`; conditional on\n[`conj:q-collatz`](#conj:q-collatz); \"$[2]_q$-contact boundary\").**\nLet $(\\mathbf{C}, A, \\tau)$ be a quantum observable universe with\nsubstrate parameter $q$ whose Frobenius–Hopf object satisfies\n$2 \\mid \\chi(A)$ — e.g. the Descartes universe, $\\chi(A) = -6$; this\nparity is what makes the $[2]_q$-divisor Kummer-removable, and\n$\\chi(A) = -6$ is a Descartes-universe property, not a general-QOU one —\nand let $\\mathcal{R}_p = (S^3 \\xrightarrow{\\pi_H} S^2, \\xi_q)$\nbe its Reeb bundle\n([Reeb bundle](#def:reeb-bundle)) with $U(1)$ fiber\nparametrized by $q = e^{i\\varTheta}$, $\\varTheta \\in [0, 2\\pi)$.\n\n### From integer parity to the $[2]_q$-divisor\n\nClassical Collatz hinges on a single question: is $n$ even\nor odd?  Parity is residue mod $2$.  The number $2$ is\nspecial: it is the smallest prime, the only even prime,\nand the denominator of the halving step $n/2$.\n\nIn the QOU, the integer $2$ lifts to the quantum integer\n$[2]_q = q + 1$ (combinatorial convention;\nsee [q-Collatz conjecture](#conj:q-collatz)).\nThe $[2]_q$-divisor is the locus where $[2]_q = 0$,\ni.e. $q = -1$:\n\n$$\n  D_{[2]}  :=  \\{q : [2]_q = 0\\}\n  =  \\{-1\\}.\n$$\n\nThis is where the $q$-analog of \"dividing by $2$\"\ndegenerates — where the halving step ceases to exist.\n\n**Kummer obstruction at the divisor.**\nThe point $q = -1$ belongs to $\\mu_2$ (the 2nd roots\nof unity).  The Kummer obstruction\n([root-of-unity truncation](#prop:root-of-unity-truncation))\nat level $n = 2$ asks: does $2$ divide $\\chi(A) = -6$?\nYes — $6/2 = 3$.  The obstruction **vanishes**.  This\nmeans the $[2]_q$-divisor is removable: the QOU axioms\ncan resolve the singularity.  At $q = -1$, the residue ring\nis $\\mathbb{Z}[q^{\\pm 1}]/(q+1) \\cong \\mathbb{Z}$\n(setting $q = -1$), and the $[2]_q$-adic valuation\nspecializes to the ordinary $2$-adic valuation.\n\n### The $[2]_q$-adic valuation as contact order\n\nFor an element $P \\in \\mathcal{S}(q) \\cong \\mathbb{Z}[q^{\\pm 1}]$\nof the Skein module, define the **$[2]_q$-adic valuation**:\n\n$$\n  v_{[2]}(P)  :=  \\max\\bigl\\{k \\geq 0 :\n  [2]_q^k \\mid P \\text{ in } \\mathbb{Z}[q^{\\pm 1}]\\bigr\\}.\n\n\n[…truncated; see manuscript for remainder…]\n\n    The Lean encoding below states the manuscript claim over a context class and discharges it from the class's fields (§3b-conditional). As of C10 the Kummer-removability half is no longer a raw axiom — it is derived from the universal obstruction-reduction (`obstruction_removable_of_even_chi` above); a full derivation of the remaining substrate primitive — the `κ₀ = χ(A)` trace-gap input inherited from `QouObstructionReductionContext` — remains pending, but is now LOCALISED rather than merely named: `QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ObstructionResidualGap` proves (i) that in the presence of `trace_pairing_cast` the three trace fields are equivalent to the single equation `κ₀ = χ(A)`, so the apparatus around it is decorative and `hattori_stallings` is the sole audit target; and (ii) that the two literature inputs (`vdb_duality`, `drinfeld_rigidity`) cannot reach it — an explicit structural core satisfies both while `κ₀ ≠ χ(A)` — although they do still force conclusion (a), `dim HH² = 1`. So closing this requires an actual Hochschild computation; no rearrangement of the existing fields will do it. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:collatz-contact-boundary","label":"prop:collatz-contact-boundary","md":"quantum-observable-universe/appendix-surreals/collatz-contact-boundary.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.obstruction_removable_of_even_chi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.obstruction_removable_of_even_chi","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/collatz_contact_boundary.lean#L56-L66","doc":"**`2 ∣ χ(A)` ⟹ the `[2]_q`-divisor is Kummer-removable — DERIVED** (formerly a\nraw context-class axiom `obstruction_removable_of_even_chi`). Removability is\nthe vanishing of the level-2 obstruction (`kummer_obstruction_removable`), and\n`kappa_vanishes_iff_chi` reduces that vanishing to `2 ∣ χ(A)`. So the parity\ncondition now discharges removability through the universal obstruction, with\nno independent assumption. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.kummer_obstruction_removable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.kummer_obstruction_removable","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/collatz_contact_boundary.lean#L48-L54","doc":"**Kummer-level-2 obstruction removable** := the level-2 Kummer obstruction\n*vanishes*. This is the manuscript's own identity — *\"the obstruction vanishes;\nthis means the `[2]_q`-divisor is removable\"* — i.e. in Kummer theory the\nobstruction class **is** the removability criterion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.CollatzContactBoundaryContext.chi_A_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.CollatzContactBoundaryContext.chi_A_eq","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/collatz_contact_boundary.lean#L46-L46","doc":"Descartes specialisation: `χ(A) = -6` (Bring's surface). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.CollatzContactBoundaryContext.q_int_2_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.CollatzContactBoundaryContext.q_int_2_eq","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/collatz_contact_boundary.lean#L44-L44","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.CollatzContactBoundaryContext.q_int_2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.CollatzContactBoundaryContext.q_int_2","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/collatz_contact_boundary.lean#L43-L43","doc":"The q-integer `[2]_q = q + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.CollatzContactBoundaryContext.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.CollatzContactBoundaryContext.q","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/collatz_contact_boundary.lean#L41-L41","doc":"Substrate parameter `q` of the QOU, over the coefficient ring `R`.\n\n**Base ring (§7c).** This was `ℝ`, and that was a gratuitous\nspecialisation: the manuscript's ambient object is the Skein module\n`𝒮(q) ≅ ℤ[q^{±1}]` — a Laurent ring — and the only thing done with `q`\nhere is the ring identity `[2]_q = q + 1` and the hypothesis\n`[2]_q = 0` (i.e. `q = -1`, the residue-ring specialisation the prose\ndescribes). No ordering, no radical, no `Real.*` construct appears, so\nper AGENTS.md §7c this belongs over a generic commutative ring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.CollatzContactBoundaryContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.CollatzContactBoundaryContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/collatz_contact_boundary.lean#L30-L30","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.CollatzContactBoundaryContext.toQouObstructionReductionContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.CollatzContactBoundaryContext.toQouObstructionReductionContext","kind":"def","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/collatz_contact_boundary.lean#L30-L46","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.CollatzContactBoundaryContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.CollatzContactBoundaryContext","kind":"class","line":23,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/collatz_contact_boundary.lean#L23-L46","doc":"QOU-furnished context for the `collatz_contact_boundary` claim. **Extends** the\nuniversal Kummer obstruction-reduction context (`QouObstructionReductionContext`,\nsupplying `χ(A)`, `κ₀`, the level-`n` vanishing predicate and its definitional\nreduction), together with the Skein/Reeb data of a quantum observable universe\n`(𝐂, A, τ)` — `q` its substrate parameter, `[2]_q = q + 1` — and the Descartes\nspecialisation `χ(A) = -6`. Kummer removability is no longer a field: it is\n*defined* below as level-2 obstruction vanishing and *derived* from parity. ","signatureChunk":0}]}